    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d155">

                <pb facs="0239" n="163" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg163"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.77/1493</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Reinsch to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-24T12:00:00+08:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 24, 1915, noon</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Managing director of Hukuang Railway agrees to accept tenders for ten locomotives
                    with alternative American standard specifications. Copies of the tenders to be
                    opened on January 15 in New York have been sent to Hunt.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
